# Route-scoped upload proxy seam (APP2-I01 §12). ADR-APP2-001.
#
# ============================== INACTIVE ==============================
# Nothing includes this file yet, and including it is APP2-B01's job.
#
# It renders to /etc/nginx/conf.d/includes/upload-proxy.conf, which nginx.conf
# never loads: its only include glob is `/etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf`, one level
# up. So this file is inert until a `location` block explicitly includes it —
# the same mechanism that keeps proxy-headers.conf opt-in.
#
# It exists now, unused, so the streaming decision lives with the storage
# foundation that requires it rather than being rediscovered under B01.
# `tools/nginx-upload-seam.test.mjs` fails if it ever becomes active early.
# ======================================================================
#
# Usage in APP2-B01 (illustrative — do NOT uncomment here):
#
#   location = /api/admin/assets/upload {
#       include /etc/nginx/conf.d/includes/proxy-headers.conf;
#       include /etc/nginx/conf.d/includes/upload-proxy.conf;
#       proxy_pass http://api_upstream;
#   }

# The single directive this seam exists to carry.
#
# Nginx buffers a whole request body to disk before contacting the upstream by
# default. That would defeat the streaming intake in ADR-APP2-001: the API
# would receive the body only after the gateway had already spooled all of it,
# so the server-side SHA-256 and the size guard could not run against a live
# stream, and a rejected upload would already have been written to gateway
# disk. Turning buffering off makes the client's stream the API's stream.
#
# Consequence B01 must handle: with buffering off, the upstream sees a body
# that can stall or abort mid-flight, so the API owns its own read timeout and
# incremental size enforcement. The gateway is not the size authority.
proxy_request_buffering off;

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ownership hooks — deliberately UNSET (APP2-I01 §4, §12)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The directives below are the route-scoped knobs this seam owns. They carry no
# value here because the values are not ours to choose yet:
#
#   client_max_body_size   blocked on the open Product Owner parameter
#                          "maximum image bytes" (STORAGE upload-size gate).
#                          Inventing a number here would silently become the
#                          product limit and contradict the API's own limit.
#
#   proxy_read_timeout     an upload holds the upstream connection open for as
#   proxy_send_timeout     long as the client streams; the gateway defaults
#                          (60s, set http-wide) are tuned for normal requests,
#                          not for a large body over a slow link. B01 sets
#                          these per route once the size limit is known —
#                          timeout and size are one decision, not two.
#
# Until then the http-level defaults from development.conf.template apply.
# B01 must add these three directives to this file (or to the including
# location) as part of the upload route, sourcing every value from the
# gateway's environment using the existing ${GATEWAY_*} pattern.
